080426B0 display-position-return

After the success branch, the position copy uses r1 through r3 and leaves the display pointer in r0.

The explicit form changed the ROM bytes. The guarded form passed the unit ROM check.

--- a/src/engine/video/display_animation.c
+++ b/src/engine/video/display_animation.c
@@ -165,5 +165,7 @@
         return -1;
     *display->position = *position;
-    /* No return on success: the ROM leaves the incoming display pointer in r0. */
+#ifdef UBFIX
+    return (s32)display; // r0 retains the incoming display pointer
+#endif
 }
 
